@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Acceptance test against a fake navigator.bluetooth
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
box "Test — Playwright on Chromium" #E0F2FE
  participant "Acceptance spec\n(Traces to: L2-xxx)" as spec
  participant "Playwright clock" as clock
  participant "FakeBluetooth" as fake
end box
box "Frontend — Stride Link page under test" #D1FADF
  participant "stride-link.html" as page
end box
spec -> clock : page.clock.install()
spec -> fake : addInitScript(installFake(scenario "unlocked")) before any page script (L2-070)
spec -> page : goto dist/stride-link.html
spec -> page : click Connect
page -> fake : requestDevice(options)
fake --> page : FakeDevice "STRIDE-8S"
page -> fake : startNotifications f3, f4; writes to f2
fake -> fake : Record { t, char, bytes } for every write
fake --> page : Scripted F0 E0 34 12 05 78 97 2A, then the acknowledgement
spec -> clock : runFor(2400); no real sleeps (L2-070)
spec -> fake : writes
fake --> spec : RecordedWrite[]
spec -> spec : Assert init order, response F0 E0 00 00 57 00 00 27, activation timing
spec -> page : Assert verdict text "Unlocked"; no pageerror or unhandledrejection (L2-058)
note over fake : The test fails if the real requestDevice is reached (L2-070).\nCI never grants Bluetooth permission (L2-071).
@enduml
